ent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"A multi-session coding agent runs in a terminal, a desktop shell or a web chat without owning an editor. It keeps many conversations, each with its own history and workspace; reads, edits, greps and runs commands in a project root behind approvals and a sandbox; delegates to subagents; persists sessions across restarts and reconnects clients to work in flight."},"1465":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-9","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"AgentKit is built for that shape at the plugin level, not the config level. createAgent and @agentkit/workspace still work for the simple case, but a product like this is a harness, and the spine is where a harness lives: createRuntime, agentRuntime(), and plugins on public extension points. Two examples prove it and are the right starting points:"},"1466":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-10","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"examples/mini-harness: a terminal coding agent with workspace tools, permissions, plan mode, compaction and a transcript UI, built from public APIs only."},"1467":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-11","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"examples/grand-tour: every battery mounted together, twenty-two verified stops, a live dashboard."},"1468":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-12","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#what-the-spine-already-provides","content":"Treat these as done. Each is an ordinary plugin or service; none patches th