ons, recall"},"1880":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-87","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"20"},"1881":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-88","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"Things a person asks the harness, not the model"},"1882":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-89","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"commands"},"1883":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-90","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"commands"},"1884":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-91","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"21"},"1885":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-92","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"A narrower world for one agent"},"1886":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-93","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"realms"},"1887":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-94","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"runtime"},"1888":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-95","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"22"},"1889":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-96","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"Change the composition without forking it"},"1890":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-97","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"bundles and patches"},"1891":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-98","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#the-stops","content":"any row"},"1892":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-99","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#how-it-is-built","content":"src/harness.ts is the whole composition: one defineBundle of rows, every row an ordinary plugin. dumpConfig prints it; a Patch edits it by id."},"1893":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-100","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#how-it-is-built","content":"src/model.ts is the scripted model. Each stop installs a responder that reads the request the runtime built (system prompt, history, tool schemas, the last tool result) and answers like a capable model would. That is documentation as much as test fixture: the responder shows what the model sees at each point."},"1894":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-101","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#how-it-is-built","content":"src/stops.ts is the tour: a prompt, a responder, and checks. Stops with no prompt drive the runtime directly (commands, realms, patches)."},"1895":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-102","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#how-it-is-built","content":"src/journal.ts turns runtime events into a timeline. The CLI prints it and the dashboard streams it over server-sent events; neither hooks into the loop."},"1896":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-103","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#how-it-is-built","content":"Row order matters and is stated in the file: the journal mounts first so it observes every tools/ask before the approver answers, and hooks mounts before approvalPolicy so a hook can veto a call before anyone is asked."},"1897":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-104","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#what-a-stop-looks-like","content":"The hook itself is one line of config in the bundle: a PreToolUse shell command that reads the call on stdin and exits non-zero to refuse it."},"1898":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-105","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#in-live-mode","content":"--live sends the same prompts to a real provider. The checks then describe what the model did rather than what it had to do; a capable model passes most of them, and a check that fails there is a model choice, not a harness defect."},"1899":{"id":"/docs/extend","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"page","content":"Extending AgentKit","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Extending"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend"},"1900":{"id":"/docs/extend-0","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend","content":"Two levels, one runtime — from a one-call agent to your own harness"},"1901":{"id":"/docs/extend-1","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend#two-levels","content":"Two levels"},"1902":{"id":"/docs/extend-2","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend#why-a-kernel","content":"Why a kernel"},"1903":{"id":"/docs/extend-3","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"Where to reach"},"1904":{"id":"/docs/extend-4","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend#packages","content":"Packages"},"1905":{"id":"/docs/extend-5","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"1906":{"id":"/docs/extend-6","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend","content":"createAgent is the one-call path: configuration goes in, an agent comes out. It covers the common case, and most projects never need anything else."},"1907":{"id":"/docs/extend-7","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend","content":"Underneath it is a plugin kernel, and the same import gives you that too. That is the difference between an SDK you configure and an SDK you build on — the second one lets you ship a coding agent, a review bot, or a domain harness without waiting for AgentKit to add a config key for it."},"1908":{"id":"/docs/extend-8","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#two-levels","content":"Both levels run the same services, the same tool pipeline, and the same session log. Level 2 is not a rewrite of level 1 — it is level 1 with the lid off."},"1909":{"id":"/docs/extend-9","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#why-a-kernel","content":"The old extension surface was a config schema, and a config schema can only express features its author already imagined. Denying a tool call, wrapping a dispatch with a deadline, rewriting what the model sees, or pointing the filesystem at a remote sandbox each meant patching the runtime."},"1910":{"id":"/docs/extend-10","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#why-a-kernel","content":"Now every part of a turn is a service (something you can replace) or an event (something you can intercept). A plugin can deny a tool call, wrap the dispatch, rewrite the prompt, swap the model adapter, add a durable event type, give one session a different tool set, or replace the loop itself — all through public APIs, none of them requiring a change to AgentKit."},"1911":{"id":"/docs/extend-11","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#why-a-kernel","content":"That is also the honesty test: AgentKit's own batteries — skills, retrieval, MCP, recall, budgets, structured output, subagents, session persistence, Code Mode — ship as plugins on this spine. Anything AgentKit does, a third party can do too."},"1912":{"id":"/docs/extend-12","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"I want to…"},"1913"