d):"},"2419":{"id":"/docs/workflows/static-57","page_id":"/docs/workflows/static","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflows/static#approvals-and-orchestration","content":"With telemetry on, a session run exports one workflow.run root (tagged with the session id), or nests under the chat turn that started it."},"2420":{"id":"/docs/workflows/static-58","page_id":"/docs/workflows/static","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflows/static#run-from-chat-workflowsexpose","content":"Set workflows: { expose: true, ... } and every session turn gets a run_workflow({ id, input }) tool whose description lists the registered workflows: id, name, description and the {{input.key}} names each one reads. The run happens in the calling session, so approvals land there too:"},"2421":{"id":"/docs/workflows/static-59","page_id":"/docs/workflows/static","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workflows/static#run-from-chat-workflowsexpose","content":"expose: true is shorthand for {}: run_workflow and list_workflows (ids, names, descriptions, input keys) are on, build_workflow is off. Pass { run?, list?, build? } to choose. build_workflow({ task, name? }) has the model draft a workflow for an ad-hoc task and runs it in the session; with a name it is also saved to the store. To draft without running, call session.generateWorkflow(task), which returns a WorkflowGraph. Unnamed build_workflow drafts and generateWorkflow drafts feed the same repeat detection as dynamic workflows, without experimental.dynamicWorkflows: when a similar task comes up a second time (taskSimilarity; repeatAfter, similarityThreshold and autoPromptSave are read from experimental.dynamicWorkflows when set), the session emits workflow:save:prompt { workflowId, suggestedName, runCount, graph } and session.saveWorkflow(workflowId, name) stores it. workflowInputKeys(def) returns the {{input.key}} names a definition reads."},"2422":{"id":"/docs/workflows/static-60","page_id":"/docs/workflows/static","tags":[],"type":"t