time ships only MemorySessionStore so it stays edge-capable. The Node-side implementations of the same seam live in @agentkit/core:"],[469,"@agentkit/server"],[1531,"@agentkit/server"],[1223,"@agentkit/server has four entry points with the same routes and hardening (body limit, random session ids, session cap, auth, tenant isolation, error mapping):"],[23,"@agentkit/svelte"],[475,"@agentkit/svelte"],[1389,"@agentkit/svelte stores"],[22,"@agentkit/vue"],[473,"@agentkit/vue"],[1427,"@agentkit/vue composables"],[477,"@agentkit/workspace"],[1272,"/answer"],[1269,"/approvals?sessionId=…"],[1266,"/approve / /reject"],[1311,"/artifacts?sessionId=…"],[1275,"/cancel"],[1233,"/capabilities"],[1257,"/events?sessionId=…"],[1260,"/events/all"],[1230,"/health"],[1530,"/health"],[1278,"/history?sessionId=…"],[1302,"/mcp"],[1308,"/mcp/:id/tools"],[1305,"/mcp/connect, /mcp/disconnect, /mcp/reload, /mcp/add, /mcp/remove, /mcp/auth"],[1281,"/mode"],[328,"/models"],[1236,"/models"],[1101,"/models/*"],[336,"/models/add"],[1242,"/models/add / /models/remove"],[332,"/models/default"],[1239,"/models/default"],[344,"/models/refresh"],[1248,"/models/refresh"],[340,"/models/test"],[1245,"/models/test"],[1251,"/models/usage"],[1099,"/rag/* (ingest posts { docs })"],[1317,"/rag/ingest, /rag/query"],[1314,"/rag/sources"],[1287,"/saveWorkflow"],[1263,"/send"],[1254,"/session"],[1284,"/todo/edit"],[2107,"/tree inside the CLI (or --tree at startup) shows what actually loaded and what any blocked plugin is still waiting for."],[1290,"/workflows, /workflows/:id"],[1293,"/workflows/:id"],[1299,"/workflows/generate"],[1296,"/workflows/run"],[1800,"#"],[1506,"~/.agentkit/settings.json, project agentkit.settings.json searched upward, flags on top"],[576,"0"],[2334,"0.82"],[35,"0.85"],[579,"1"],[1804,"1"],[1840,"10"],[1844,"11"],[1848,"12"],[1852,"13"],[1856,"14"],[1860,"15"],[1864,"16"],[1868,"17"],[1872,"18"],[1876,"19"],[582,"2"],[1808,"2"],[2331,"2"],[121,"2 retries, 500ms→8s backoff"],[1880,"20"],[178,"2048"],[1884,"21"],[1888,"22"],[585,"3"],[1812,"3"],[1816,"4"],[1367,"404 on /events: session expired server-side; POST /session again."],[1820,"5"],[1824,"6"],[1828,"7"],[1832,"8"],[1836,"9"],[1857,"A big catalogue the model discovers when it needs it"],[1557,"A bundle is the same composition expressed as data: an ordered list of rows, each with an id."],[763,"A catalogue in the system prompt: one line per MCP server or category, with a count and\nexample names, so the model knows what exists:\n- github (40): list_issues, create_pull_request, …"],[1869,"A ceiling the loop does not know about"],[670,"A Claude-style chat app (Next.js UI + a small Node agent server) that uses every feature in one place: thinking, tools, approvals, questions, Plan mode, a sandboxed workspace, MCP management, workflows and telemetry. It runs offline on a scripted mock or live on any provider key in .env."],[1106,"A ClientSession for id (the same object per id): every call carries id, on / onAny see that session's events plus agent-wide ones (MCP, models) from the shared stream, send / answer emit client:send / client:answer, workflows.run closes the run in the hub's state when it returns. Pass it to any store or hook. Its close() detaches its listeners only"],[729,"A command that exits non-zero comes back with its exit code and output for the model, marked isError: true with the line that explains it (exited with code 1: Error: Cannot find module …), so it shows as a failed call in traces."],[1551,"A composition as data, so someone else can retune it without forking you"],[1446,"a computed list of audit rows"],[1450,"a computed plan"],[2052,"A config that fails to parse fails that plugin's fiber and leaves the rest of the tree running — one bad row does not take down the harness."],[2015,"A context with services"],[1987,"a ctx.credentials provider"],[1953,"a ctx.shell provider"],[1951,"a ctx.terminals backend + terminalTools"],[1961,"a ctx.web / ctx.lsp provider"],[2342,"a cycle, a bad id or an empty/oversized graph rejects the draft."],[2197,"A decision is { kind: \"allow\" }, { kind: \"deny\", reason }, or { kind: \"ask\", question }. The runtime — not your plugin — runs the tools/ask serial when a listener answers ask, so asking and answering stay independently replaceable."],[1749,"A deferred tool stays registered and callable, so ctx.tools.execute and\nCode Mode still reach it. What changes is ctx.tools.schemas()."],[2030,"A dependency here is a relationship over time, not a startup-order constraint. The plugin loads when its dependencies appear, unloads when one disappears, and reloads when it comes back."],[1630,"A grep matching four thousand lines is not a bug — the answer really is four thousand lines. Truncating throws away what the model needed; inlining costs the window. Spilling keeps the whole result addressable and returns a head plus a locator."],[1675,"A hook is not a plugin: it is a line of config pointing at a script. That is the whole point — \"run the formatter after every edit\" or \"never let it touch .env\" should not require writing TypeScript, publishing a package, or restarting anything."],[1536,"A job queue with retries and priority. ctx.jobs runs work in the background; a durable queue across restarts is a product choice (pg-boss, BullMQ, or a small table)."],[1561,"A later bundle re-declaring an id overrides that row in place rather than appending a duplicate, so extends composes without reordering surprises."],[1825,"A line of config can veto a tool"],[1634,"A loop lets the model choose the next action; a workflow fixes it in advance. Both are useful, and the mistake is making one pretend to be the other. Steps declare needs, so independent ones run concurrently without the author scheduling anything."],[1674,"A malformed settings file fails loudly at load. Silently ignoring it would mean a typo'd JSON file makes a policy quietly stop applying — the failure mode worth the least tolerance."],[1461,"A minimal v1"],[2076,"a mode changes the visible tool set and the prompt, per agent"],[1644,"A model that can only make one tool call per step spends a step filtering a list, another chaining a result into the next call, and a third summarising. Code Mode collapses that: every visible tool becomes await tools.<name>(args) inside a single run_code program."],[1464,"A multi-session coding agent runs in a terminal, a desktop shell or a web chat without owning an editor. It keeps many conversations, each with its own history and workspace; reads, edits, greps and runs commands in a project root behind approvals and a sandbox; delegates to subagents; persists sessions across restarts and reconnects clients to work in flight."],[1885,"A narrower world for one agent"],[1606,"A one-shot shell loses everything between calls: a cd, an activated virtualenv, an SSH session, a REPL. That is the right default — reproducible and cheap — which is exactly why the stateful case needs its own seam rather than a flag on the stateless one."],[1558,"A patch targets a row by id and applies in order, so a deployment tunes a composition it does not own:"],[2262,"A pending call renders as generic, terminal, or diff. A completed call adds search and web:"],[1849,"A plan the UI can render"],[2051,"A plugin may declare a schema. Zod works directly, and so does anything else with a parse:"],[2227,"A plugin that needs durable state extends the event map and says how the model should see it:"],[1518,"A policy listener, so no tool can forget it"],[2120,"A policy plugin, end to end"],[1728,"a prompt section"],[1760,"A prompt section lists the catalogue: every tool with a short description, or, past 30\ndeferred tools, one line per MCP server or category with a count and example names.\nctx.tools.defer(predicate) is the registry primitive underneath; a realm inherits its\nparent's deferrals and cannot undo them. createAgent has the same behaviour built in as\ntoolSearch."],[1544,"A published CLI. mini-harness is the reference; promoting it to a package with the settings-files convention is packaging, not runtime work."],[2091,"a read-only researcher in its own tool realm, delegated to through one task tool"],[1500,"A registry with its own waterfall, no model turn"],[1527,"A seam and a tool; bring a provider"],[1691,"A seam rather than scattered process.env reads, for three reasons: a hosted deployment usually has a vault instead of an environment, a missing key should be one clear failure rather than an adapter-specific one, and a value that never becomes a plain property is much harder to log by accident."],[764,"A search_tools tool: the model asks for what it needs (\"post to slack\", \"github\") and\nthe best matches become callable on its next step, with their full definitions."],[1556,"A sequence of runtime.plugin() calls is a program. You can read it, but you cannot address a line of it from outside — so a consumer who wants one row changed has to fork the package that published it."],[2049,"A service is read through the reader's own context, so a registration made inside a service method belongs to the calling plugin:"],[2026,"A service published at ctx.<name> is reachable by every plugin in the tree. Augment the Services interface to type it:"],[1560,"A set or replace against a row that is not there throws rather than silently doing nothing. A composition you cannot trust to have applied is worse than no composition at all — a typo in an id should not become a security policy that quietly stopped applying. (remove of an absent id is a no-op, since \"make sure this is gone\" is already satisfied.)"],[1017,"A single run can use another model without changing the default: session.send(input, { model: \"fast\" }) takes a registry id or a provider/model id."],[1424,"A store listens to the session only while something is subscribed. See Streaming & wire protocol for endpoints and event types."],[1134,"A store takes a ClientSession (from connect() or hub.session(id)) or a bare event source ({ onAny }, e.g. streamAll()): without a session the state follows the events and the actions reject with \"Session not connected\"."],[2056,"A terminal coding agent built only from public plugin APIs"],[1784,"A tool calls ctx.fs.readFile(path); it does not know whether that lands on a local disk, a container, or an object store. That indirection is the point — a tool written for a laptop runs unmodified against a remote sandbox."],[1735,"A tool can say what it does to the world:"],[1813,"A tool has a value, a rendering and a card"],[2247,"A tool has four audiences and they want different things. The runtime validates arguments, code consumes a canonical value, the model reads prose, and a UI renders a card. Collapsing those into one string is what makes tool output either unusable by code or unreadable by the model."],[2340,"a tool node naming a tool the agent does not have becomes an AI node;"],[2252,"A tool that already publishes its own model-facing schema — an MCP server, for instance — passes it as jsonSchema and owns its own validation, rather than having one derived from a placeholder Zod type."],[1927,"a tools/execute listener"],[1929,"a tools/post-execute listener"],[1923,"a tools/pre-execute listener, or approvalPolicy by annotation"],[2088,"a UI that imports no tool, and gets new tools' cards for free"],[2250,"A value that describes a failure — a command's non-zero exit — can still be returned rather than thrown: output.isError(args, value) marks the result isError while the model reads the rendered value as usual. bashTool does this for a non-zero exit, so the session log, UIs, workflows and Code Mode see the command fail."],[633,"A: structured run()"],[249,"Abort the run"],[248,"AbortSignal"],[190,"access"],[1396,"Actions"],[2141,"adapter registration and streaming"],[751,"Adaptive TOON/JSON/CSV encoding and context compaction"],[1243,"Add (BYOK) or remove a model (when userConfigurable)"],[1914,"add a capability"],[1954,"add a human command that costs no model turn"],[540,"Add BYOK model"],[1936,"add durable state that survives a reload"],[1930,"add model-facing context"],[1546,"Add your own tools with defineHarnessTool, your own prompt sections, and a tools/ask responder that talks to your UI. Everything above runs on the mock provider for tests, and dumpConfig-style printing with describeBundle shows anyone what you shipped."],[2217,"Adding a durable fact"],[134,"Adds a handoff_to_human tool; calling it stops the run, emits handoff:request and sets result.handoff"],[502,"Adjust ../agentkit to your clone path, then:"],[495,"After editing AgentKit, rebuild and restart your app:"],[2027,"After that, ctx.tools is typed everywhere, with no registry lookup and no casts."],[2345,"After workflow:save:prompt, persist via session:"],[367,"Agent"],[1234,"Agent capability flags + enriched models block"],[752,"Agent config"],[257,"Agent methods: run, session, on, setMode, mcp, models, workflow, workflows, capabilities."],[2115,"Agent runtime"],[2001,"Agent runtime — services, the turn, every extension point"],[2053,"Agent runtime — the services and extension points built on this"],[2238,"Agent runtime — where the log sits in a turn"],[1222,"Agent URLs in the examples: express-api serves page and agent on :8787 (agent at /api/agent), nextjs-chat mounts the agent in its own route (/api/agent on :3001), vanilla-js-ui serves both on :3001. Workflow UI uses :8788."],[365,"Agent, session, events, and modes"],[309,"agent:spawned, agent:done, agent:handoff"],[2375,"agent.capabilities().workflows is true when the store exists."],[840,"agent.mcp.tools() returns { name, serverId, description?, jsonSchema? } for each callable tool. Stdio servers take env: { KEY: \"value\" }, merged over the parent's environment. Leave a whole server out of one run with send(input, { tools: { deny: [\"<serverId>__*\"] } })."],[541,"agent.models.add({…})"],[529,"agent.models.list()"],[545,"agent.models.refresh()"],[533,"agent.models.setDefault(id)"],[537,"agent.models.test(id)"],[549,"agent.models.usage()"],[9,"agent.run(task, opts?)"],[380,"agent.session() is interactive: send, stream, on, approve, answer, cancel, close, setMode. Use this for chat UIs and long-running work with human gates. agent.setMode() applies to subsequent run() calls on the same agent instance."],[10,"agent.session(opts?) / agent.mcp"],[271,"agent.stream(task, opts?) and session.stream(input, opts?) return an AgentStream — an async-iterable of every AgentEvent, plus a result promise. The iterator ends on the terminal done/error event; stream.cancel() unsubscribes (and cancels the underlying run for a session.stream()). streamToConsole(stream, opts?) renders a live run to the terminal (TTY/NO_COLOR-aware). attachConsole(sessionOrAgent, { events?, color?, out? }) prints the same view for everything a session or agent emits and returns a detach function."],[2406,"agent.workflows.delete(id)"],[2400,"agent.workflows.get(id)"],[2398,"agent.workflows.list()"],[2402,"agent.workflows.run(id, input?)"],[2154,"agent/pre-step"],[2081,"agent/pre-step + context/compacted"],[2093,"agent/pre-step + tools/pre-execute"],[1719,"agent/pre-step, agent/request-error, context/compacted"],[2157,"agent/request"],[2160,"agent/request-error"],[2163,"agent/turn-stopping"],[1488,"AgentHandle.status, an inbox, followup(), steer(), cancel()"],[823,"AgentKit connects to external MCP servers at agent startup and merges their capabilities with your own Zod tools. MCP resources and source-classified tools feed read-only context; callable tools are namespaced as serverId__toolName and run through the same approval and reasoning loop as developer tools."],[377,"AgentKit has a configured level and a compositional one. createAgent(config) is the first: configuration in, agent out. Under it is a plugin kernel where every part of a turn is a service you can replace or an event you can intercept — see Extending AgentKit. The concepts below describe the configured level; both run the same tool pipeline and the same session log."],[427,"AgentKit headless agent runtime"],[414,"AgentKit is a headless TypeScript agent runtime. createAgent(config) validates config with Zod at construction. The engine ships providers (Anthropic, OpenAI, Ollama, Gemini, Mistral, Groq, mock), tools, memory, MCP, workflows, and adaptive encoding."],[431,"AgentKit is a TypeScript agent runtime you import into existing projects. The engine runs on Node; any UI connects over the AG-UI wire."],[1465,"AgentKit is built for that shape at the plugin level, not the config level. createAgent and @agentkit/workspace still work for the simple case, but a product like this is a harness, and the spine is where a harness lives: createRuntime, agentRuntime(), and plugins on public extension points. Two examples prove it and are the right starting points:"],[418,"AgentKit ships a single-file guide written for AI coding assistants: every feature, the full config, events, the server/client/hook APIs and recipes. Install it into your project and your assistant builds with the SDK instead of hand-rolling servers, reconnects or approval queues:"],[605,"AgentKit Studio (studio)"],[799,"AgentKit surfaces runtime activity as typed AG-UI events rather than only stdout. Set logging.level to control log emissions from the agent shell, and subscribe to cost:update for per-turn token and cost estimates from the active provider."],[572,"AgentKit uses config over code at every level:"],[245,"AgentMode"],[1734,"AgentOptions"],[2204,"agentRuntime() deliberately mounts only the spine. These ship alongside it and are opt-in, because each one is a policy choice rather than a default:"],[2127,"agentRuntime() is six ctx.plugin() calls. Copy them and swap any one — nothing in it is privileged."],[2143,"agents"],[291,"Agents this one may transfer to (default: all others)"],[1486,"agents.create({ sessionId, model, mode, maxSteps, meta })"],[1509,"AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md in the prompt, read through the filesystem seam"],[2079,"AGENTS.md support in twelve lines"],[2383,"AI"],[2344,"AI nodes run without tools and do not stream stream:token; the session's done carries the last node's output, and each node's result is on workflow:step:done.output. With telemetry on, each run is one trace: a workflow.run root (generated: true, workflowId, workflowName) with the node spans under it, so it appears on the admin Workflows page."],[166,"AI-generated DAG workflows (unstable)"],[2399,"All definitions"],[802,"All events stream over SSE — see Streaming. No separate logging HTTP API."],[1184,"All hooks accept null while connecting and return empty state; a new session starts fresh. They take a ClientSession, a hub's hub.session(id), or a bare event source ({ onAny }, e.g. streamAll(); actions then reject)."],[385,"All subsystems publish to one typed event bus. Subscribe with agent.on or session.on. The same events map to AG-UI on the wire via @agentkit/server."],[1688,"allow"],[2174,"allow / deny / ask — the policy layer"],[1922,"allow / deny / ask on a tool call"],[201,"Allow run_command outbound network"],[1761,"allow wins over requireApproval. deny is registered as a guard, so no\nlater tools/pre-execute listener, however permissive, can lift it. A\ntool with delegates: true (call_tool, create_subagent) is passed\nthrough: the calls it makes are gated one by one. Questions go out on\ntools/ask; with no responder mounted, the call is declined."],[1497,"Allow, ask, deny by what a tool declares, plus shell-script hooks"],[1821,"Allow, ask, deny, by what a tool declares"],[199,"allowNetwork"],[1614,"allowParallelInProgress is required with no default: it changes the tool description the model reads, and a harness should state which working style it wants rather than inherit one."],[202,"allowSensitiveReads"],[1135,"Also available: workflowRunStore (run, generate, save, dismissSavePrompt), workflowsStore (refresh, load, remove, save), mcpStore (server actions), usageStore,