tive module, and making the runtime need a compiler to get a bash tool is a bad trade. Pipes keep cwd and exported environment — which is the reason to want a persistent session at all. What they do not give you is a TTY: no job control, no line editing, and programs checking isatty() take their non-interactive branch. Mount a node-pty-backed provider when a session needs those; the tools do not change."],[1603,"nodeTerminals, scriptedTerminals()"],[1689,"Non-JSON stdout becoming context rather than an error matters: echo is what people reach for first, and a stray one must not read as a refusal. A Stop hook that denies is asking for another step — that is how a \"did you run the tests?\" gate keeps the agent working."],[61,"none"],[97,"none"],[101,"none"],[125,"none"],[129,"none"],[161,"none"],[169,"none"],[1006,"none"],[1705,"Not ported, and why"],[386,"Notable groups: stream:* and thinking:* for model output, tool:* / mcp:tool:* for tool calls, plan:* / todo:* for plan mode, cost:update and log for observability, mode:changed for runtime mode switches."],[1618,"note"],[213,"Notes"],[864,"Notes"],[1910,"Now every part of a turn is a service (something you can replace) or an event (something you can intercept). A plugin can deny a tool call, wrap the dispatch, rewrite the prompt, swap the model adapter, add a durable event type, give one session a different tool set, or replace the loop itself — all through public APIs, none of them requiring a change to AgentKit."],[454,"npm"],[446,"npm registry (production)"],[511,"npm registry after publish"],[483,"npm uses the same URL form:"],[293,"number"],[996,"NVIDIA API catalog (build.nvidia.com)"],[987,"NVIDIA Nemotron runs on several hosts, and AgentKit supports each of them. Pick one in config; nothing else in your agent changes."],[998,"NVIDIA_API_KEY"],[931,"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b (Nebius Token Factory)"],[933,"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b (NVIDIA API catalog or your NIM)"],[905,"Object config: routing