ber tree, including any plugin still blocked on a dependency. Between them, \"why is my plugin not doing anything\" is usually a one-line answer."],[2099,"the fs + subprocess seams"],[1635,"The graph is validated in register(), not at run time — a cycle or a dangling needs is a mistake in the definition, and it should fail while its author is looking at it."],[1678,"the harness does"],[1897,"The hook itself is one line of config in the bundle: a PreToolUse shell command that reads the call on stdin and exits non-zero to refuse it."],[1012,"The ids live in NEMOTRON_MODELS. Any other OpenAI-compatible host that serves Nemotron (OpenRouter, vLLM, your gateway) works through registerProvider as shown below. createNvidiaProvider({ apiKey?, baseURL? }) builds the NVIDIA provider directly."],[1193,"the ids the hub knows"],[2216,"The invariant"],[383,"The iterator ends on the terminal done/error event; on failure stream.result rejects. Breaking out of the loop (or stream.cancel()) unsubscribes — on a session.stream(), cancel() also cancels the underlying run. For a ready-made terminal view, pass the stream to streamToConsole(...)."],[1584,"The kernel and the runtime give you a turn. What makes it a harness is the capability layer on top: the things an agent can actually do, each behind a seam so you can swap the implementation without touching the tools."],[2104,"The last four ship from @agentkit/core — they are not example code, they are the batteries, mounted the same way yours would be."],[762,"The likely tools: the best keyword matches between the task and each tool's name,\nargument names and description (6 by default), plus anything in alwaysLoad and any tool the\nrun or session allows by name (tools.allow)."],[1615,"The list is not projected into model history. It reaches the model as a prompt section rendering current state, so a hundred edits cost one rendering, while the log still holds every revision for a UI to replay."],[2060,"The live smoke test"],[1877,"The log is the memory"],[2097,"the log survives a restart, so fork and resume are real"],[936,"The model registry resolves the active provider and model on every session.send() and agent.run(). Call agent.models.setDefault(modelId) (or the wire/client equivalent) and the next turn uses the new model — no manual provider re-instantiation."],[1521,"The model writes a program against the tool bindings"],[1639,"The model writes a program instead of a call — and where that program runs is a seam"],[1841,"The model writes its own delegates, in parallel"],[1909,"The old extension surface was a config schema, and a config schema can only express features its author already imagined. Denying a tool call, wrapping a dispatch with a deadline, rewriting what the model sees, or pointing the filesystem at a remote sandbox each meant patching the runtime."],[1788,"The ordering is the security property. A subprocess/spawn listener can vet or rewrite a command, but the sandbox rewrite happens last, so no plugin can rewrite its way out of it — and swapping the spawner provider does not drop the confinement."],[1136,"The package ships a dependency-free ES module build, so no bundler is needed:"],[769,"The plugin kernel has the same behaviour through deferredTools; see\nContext engineering."],[801,"The reasoning loop also emits log at info level for tool starts (see orchestrator/loop.ts). Sessions emit log on cancel."],[1035,"The runtime prepends a block like:"],[419,"The same guide is LLM_GUIDE.md in the repo."],[1763,"The same path handles a provider's \"context window exceeded\" error: compact,\nthen let the loop retry. compaction/done reports what happened."],[357,"The same state composables as React, plus useModels"],[1677,"the script does"],[1571,"The services a harness is actually made of — shells, jobs, commands, todos, web, LSP and the rest"],[2223,"The session log is an append-only event log, and model history is a projection of it. That is the whole design, and everything else on